From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Torokhov <dtor@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 6 Oct 2016 16:14:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] cgroup: let CAP_SYS_NICE move other users' tasks between v1
 cgroups

Android expects system_server to be able to move tasks between different
cgroups/cpusets, but does not want to be running as root. Let's relax
permission check so that processes can move other tasks if they have
CAP_SYS_NICE in the affected task's user namespace.

Signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov <dtor@chromium.org>
[AmitP: Refactored original changes to align with upstream commit
        201af4c0fab0 ("cgroup: move cgroup files under kernel/cgroup/")]
Signed-off-by: Amit Pundir <amit.pundir@linaro.org>
(cherry picked from commit a88f61676008, which the Android common
kernel android17-6.18 carries again as eba773ab53d0 after two reverts,
and which was commit ec54762b84a1 of the Chromium OS kernel)
[Adapted to 6.18.54: the relaxation is keyed on the new
CONFIG_CGROUP_V1_ATTACH_SYS_NICE, so only a guest that enables it,
which is Android, gets it. The capability is tested on the credentials
of the file's opener, as the user ID tests above it are, and not on
those of the writer: a process without CAP_SYS_NICE cannot hand an open
file to one that has it.]

Without it every move system_server makes fails with EACCES, which
libprocessgroup logs as "AddTidToCgroup failed ... Permission denied":
an app keeps the cpu and cpuset groups its zygote child gave it at
startup and never leaves top-app for background.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 init/Kconfig              | 15 +++++++++++++++
 kernel/cgroup/cgroup-v1.c |  4 +++-
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/init/Kconfig b/init/Kconfig
index 1858e55bfd7cde401a0109369d513997d88be51d..86890b5206971ffd9decf8847a078600a5e8fae0 100644
--- a/init/Kconfig
+++ b/init/Kconfig
@@ -1031,6 +1031,21 @@ config CGROUP_FAVOR_DYNMODS
 
           Say N if unsure.
 
+config CGROUP_V1_ATTACH_SYS_NICE
+	bool "Let CAP_SYS_NICE move other users' tasks between v1 cgroups"
+	help
+	  A process may move another user's task into a cgroup of a v1
+	  hierarchy only if it is root or has the task's user ID. This option
+	  also lets a process whose file credentials hold CAP_SYS_NICE in the
+	  task's user namespace do it.
+
+	  Android's system_server moves apps between the cpu, cpuset and blkio
+	  groups of its scheduling classes without running as root. Without
+	  the option every such move fails with EACCES, and an app keeps the
+	  groups its zygote child gave it at startup.
+
+	  Say N unless the guest is Android.
+
 config MEMCG
 	bool "Memory controller"
 	select PAGE_COUNTER
diff --git a/kernel/cgroup/cgroup-v1.c b/kernel/cgroup/cgroup-v1.c
index a9e029b570c8c8c78a96e776232fac807066c8b4..f8dad2381872f26c555d19541776eb63ec705bb3 100644
--- a/kernel/cgroup/cgroup-v1.c
+++ b/kernel/cgroup/cgroup-v1.c
@@ -523,7 +523,9 @@ static ssize_t __cgroup1_procs_write(struct kernfs_open_file *of,
 	tcred = get_task_cred(task);
 	if (!uid_eq(cred->euid, GLOBAL_ROOT_UID) &&
 	    !uid_eq(cred->euid, tcred->uid) &&
-	    !uid_eq(cred->euid, tcred->suid))
+	    !uid_eq(cred->euid, tcred->suid) &&
+	    !(IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CGROUP_V1_ATTACH_SYS_NICE) &&
+	      file_ns_capable(of->file, tcred->user_ns, CAP_SYS_NICE)))
 		ret = -EACCES;
 	put_cred(tcred);
 	if (ret)
